{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For the bed.</b> That it is below in the bed." "<b>Too short to stretch out.</b> From being spread out and the extension of the curtain, like ושרוע וקלוט (Leviticus 22:23)." "<b>And the covering.</b> Like covering." "<b>As when gathered.</b> The noun of the binyan is from the paradigm of לך כנוס (Esther 4:16), and the meaning of כהתכנס is when many gather together under it, and this is a parable concerning the people and their rulers."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:38.979900418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}